    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An alkyl polyglycol ether of LAURYL ALCOHOL, chemically defined as an alcohol ethoxylate having an average alkyl chain of 12–14 carbon atoms, and an ethylene oxide chain of 9 ethylene oxide units. It is used as a detergent, and medically as a local anesthetic, and as a sclerosing agent for the treatment of ESOPHAGEAL AND GASTRIC VARICES and VARICOSE VEINS." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D000077423" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000077430>
