    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A brominating agent that replaces hydrogen atoms in benzylic or allylic positions. It is used in the oxidation of secondary alcohols to ketones and in controlled low-energy brominations. (From Miall's Dictionary of Chemistry, 5th ed; Hawley's Condensed Chemical Dictionary, 12th ed,)." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D001974" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D001975>
