    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agent with analgesic, antipyretic, and anti-inflammatory properties" ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007052" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007065>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Idoxuridine" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/XQFRJNBWHJMXHO-RRKCRQDMSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An analog of DEOXYURIDINE that inhibits viral DNA synthesis. The drug is used as an antiviral agent." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007065" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007069>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ifosfamide" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/HOMGKSMUEGBAAB-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Positional isomer of CYCLOPHOSPHAMIDE which is active as an alkylating agent and an immunosuppressive agent." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007069" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007099>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Imipramine" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/BCGWQEUPMDMJNV-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The prototypical tricyclic antidepressant. It has been used in major depression, dysthymia, bipolar depression, attention-deficit disorders, agoraphobia, and panic disorders. It has less sedative effect than some other members of this therapeutic group." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007099" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007190>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indapamide" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/NDDAHWYSQHTHNT-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A benzamide-sulfonamide-indole derived DIURETIC that functions by inhibiting SODIUM CHLORIDE SYMPORTERS." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007190" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007200>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indican" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/BXFFHSIDQOFMLE-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A substance occurring in the urine of mammals and also in blood plasma as the normal metabolite of tryptophan. An increased urinary excretion of indican is seen in Hartnup disease from the bacterial degradation of unabsorbed tryptophan." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007200" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007203>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indigo Carmine" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/KHLVKKOJDHCJMG-UHFFFAOYSA-L> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Indolesulfonic acid used as a dye in renal function testing for the detection of nitrates and chlorates, and in the testing of milk." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007203" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007204>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indium" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/APFVFJFRJDLVQX-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A metallic element, atomic number 49, atomic weight 114.818, symbol In. It is named from its blue line in the spectrum." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007204" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007208>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indocyanine Green" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/MOFVSTNWEDAEEK-UHFFFAOYSA-M> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A tricarbocyanine dye that is used diagnostically in liver function tests and to determine blood volume and cardiac output." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007208" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007213>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indomethacin" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/CGIGDMFJXJATDK-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A non-steroidal anti-inflammatory agent (NSAID) that inhibits CYCLOOXYGENASE, which is necessary for the formation of PROSTAGLANDINS and other AUTACOIDS. It also inhibits the motility of POLYMORPHONUCLEAR LEUKOCYTES." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007213" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007216>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indoprofen" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/RJMIEHBSYVWVIN-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A drug that has analgesic and anti-inflammatory properties. Following reports of adverse reactions including reports of carcinogenicity in animal studies it was withdrawn from the market worldwide. (From Martindale, The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p21)" ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007216" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007217>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Indoramin" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/JXZZEXZZKAWDSP-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An alpha-1 adrenergic antagonist that is commonly used as an antihypertensive agent." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007217" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007288>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inosine" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/UGQMRVRMYYASKQ-KQYNXXCUSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A purine nucleoside that has hypoxanthine linked by the N9 nitrogen to the C1 carbon of ribose. It is an intermediate in the degradation of purines and purine nucleosides to uric acid and in pathways of purine salvage. It also occurs in the anticodon of certain transfer RNA molecules. (Dorland, 28th ed)" ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007288" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007290>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inosine Diphosphate" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/JPXZQMKKFWMMGK-KQYNXXCUSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An inosine nucleotide containing a pyrophosphate group esterified to C5 of the sugar moiety." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007290" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007291>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inosine Monophosphate" ;
