    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A low-osmolar, ionic contrast medium used in various radiographic procedures." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007485" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007487>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Ipodate" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/YQNFBOJPTAXAKV-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Ionic monomeric contrast media. Usually the sodium or calcium salts are used for examination of the gall bladder and biliary tract. (From Martindale, The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p704)" ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007487" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007488>
