    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A metallic element with atomic symbol Fe, atomic number 26, and atomic weight 55.85. It is an essential constituent of HEMOGLOBINS; CYTOCHROMES; and IRON-BINDING PROTEINS. It plays a role in cellular redox reactions and in the transport of OXYGEN." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D007501" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D007510>
