    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A phenothiazine with pharmacological activity similar to that of both CHLORPROMAZINE and PROMETHAZINE. It has the histamine-antagonist properties of the antihistamines together with CENTRAL NERVOUS SYSTEM effects resembling those of chlorpromazine. (From Martindale, The Extra Pharmacopoeia, 30th ed, p604)" ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D008728" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008729>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Methoxamine" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/WJAJPNHVVFWKKL-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An alpha-1 adrenergic agonist that causes prolonged peripheral VASOCONSTRICTION." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D008729" .

