    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A norepinephrine derivative used as a vasoconstrictor agent." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D008771" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008773>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Methylphenazonium Methosulfate" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/RXGJTUSBYWCRBK-UHFFFAOYSA-M> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Used as an electron carrier in place of the flavine enzyme of Warburg in the hexosemonophosphate system and also in the preparation of SUCCINIC DEHYDROGENASE." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D008773" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008774>
    a <http://semanticscience.org/resource/SIO_010004> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Methylphenidate" ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <https://identifiers.org/inchikey/DUGOZIWVEXMGBE-UHFFFAOYSA-N> ;
    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A central nervous system stimulant used most commonly in the treatment of ATTENTION DEFICIT DISORDER in children and for NARCOLEPSY. Its mechanisms appear to be similar to those of DEXTROAMPHETAMINE. The d-isomer of this drug is referred to as DEXMETHYLPHENIDATE HYDROCHLORIDE." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D008774" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D008775>
