    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A short-acting benzodiazepine used in the treatment of insomnia. Some countries temporarily withdrew triazolam from the market because of concerns about adverse reactions, mostly psychological, associated with higher dose ranges. Its use at lower doses with appropriate care and labeling has been reaffirmed by the FDA and most other countries." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D014229" .

