    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The isotopic compound of hydrogen of mass 2 (deuterium) with oxygen. (From Grant & Hackh's Chemical Dictionary, 5th ed) It is used to study mechanisms and rates of chemical or nuclear reactions, as well as biological processes." ;
    <https://schema.org/identifier> "D017666" .

<https://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D017693>
